{"cluster_id": "C-0132", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B002-146"], "canonical_claim": "RESURRECT-REUPLOAD-ORPHAN is prevented by tracking the `(hash, token)` incarnation so a replacement token starts a fresh condemnation cycle.", "issue_ids": ["RESURRECT-REUPLOAD-ORPHAN"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-12-cas-archaeology/06-tests.md#3-regression-pin-archaeology-bug-ids-invariant-encoded"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0133", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B006-021"], "canonical_claim": "Probe cleanup must be HEAD-gated before issuing `deleteExact`; otherwise AWS returns 400 `InvalidArgument` when cleanup sends an empty `If-Match` after the probe keys were already deleted.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-real-s3-validation.md#L32-L33"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0134", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-109", "B005-096", "B006-028"], "canonical_claim": "GCS `CompleteMultipartUpload` silently ignores `x-goog-if-generation-match`, so conditional writes must not use multipart there; `Compose` enforces the precondition, making multipart-to-temp-key followed by `Compose(temp -> final)` and temp deletion the production path for large blobs. GCS `CompleteMultipartUpload` silently ignores `x-goog-if-generation-match`, while `Compose` enforces it; conditional writes therefore must not use multipart finalize, with unconditional multipart to a temporary key followed by conditional `Compose` as the production-grade large-blob path. On GCS, `CompleteMultipartUpload` silently ignores `x-goog-if-generation-match` (both a `0`-against-existing and a wrong-generation precondition return 200 and overwrite), so conditional writes must not use multipart on GCS; `Compose` does enforce the precondition, so the production-grade large-blob path on GCS is: unconditional multipart-to-temporary-key, then a preconditioned `Compose(temp -> final)`, then delete the temp key.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-03-cas-gcs-generation-binding-design.md#measured-ground-truth-live-bucket-2026-07-03", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-real-s3-validation.md#L60-L65", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-real-s3-validation.md#gcs-measurement"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0135", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-111", "B006-031"], "canonical_claim": "On GCS, non-numeric probe wrong tokens caused the dialect format guard to fail closed; LIST-derived MD5 ETags poisoned `If-Match` in GC and are disabled on generation stores; and `Expect: 100-continue` initially missed the dialect header, creating a B118-class stall risk. Three bugs were found and fixed while validating the GCS Generation binding end-to-end: (1) probe wrong-tokens were non-numeric, so the dialect's format guard killed the mount; (2) LIST-derived tokens on GCS are MD5 ETags (XML LIST bodies are not rewritten to generations), which would poison `If-Match` in GC, so list-derived tokens are disabled on generation-token stores; (3) the `Expect: 100-continue` handling did not recognize the GCS dialect header, creating a B118-class stall risk.", "issue_ids": ["B118"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-real-s3-validation.md#L79-L82", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-real-s3-validation.md#gcs-cycle"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0136", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B006-034", "B034-061", "B035-018"], "canonical_claim": "The CAS write path spills the entire object to local `cas_scratch` for hash-before-upload, so writing a part requires free local disk at least as large as the part even though the S3 upload streams; the proposed fix is in-stream hashing.; The CA write path historically spilled an entire part to `disks/ca/cas_scratch` before S3 upload: a 24 GiB part used about 24 GiB scratch and a 100 GiB part used about 93 GiB, so a part larger than local scratch was unwritable despite bounded RSS. Additionally, A CA write path can spill an entire 100 GiB merge to approximately 93 GiB of local scratch, so very large parts require streaming hash support or documented S3-native staging.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/BACKLOG.md#scale-findings", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-scenarios-full-scale-campaign.md#L34-L38", "utils/ca-soak/scenarios/BACKLOG.md#L744-L761"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0137", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B006-051", "B006-052"], "canonical_claim": "`Build::copyForwardFromCondemned` incorrectly verified payloads with one-shot `CityHash128`, while the pool uses streaming `HashingWriteBuffer` hashing in 2048-byte blocks (`DBMS_DEFAULT_HASHING_BLOCK_SIZE`); payloads larger than 2048 bytes were falsely rejected. Copy-forward verification must recompute the content hash with `HashingReadBuffer` over the payload and the same `getHexUIntLowercase` to `hexToU128` conversion used by the write path.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-03-unattended-night.md#L26-L38"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0138", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B007-021"], "canonical_claim": "P4 was an S3 multipart completion failure where 48 ETags were rejected after a writer kill, suggesting stale multipart-session reuse across incarnations.", "issue_ids": ["P4"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-06-cas-night-findings-fix-plan-design.md#re-audit"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0139", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B007-058"], "canonical_claim": "The S13 merge-finalize retry path re-uploaded blobs on every attempt during persistent 503s, growing the pool by 47 GB in eight minutes after the workload stopped.", "issue_ids": ["F2b", "S13"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-06-scenario-validation-night.md#task6"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0140", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B007-081"], "canonical_claim": "When token A was condemned and a writer re-uploaded token B at the same blob key, exact-token deletion of A found B and no-op'd, while the hash-keyed fold failed to condemn B, leaving B orphaned.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-07-cas-resurrect-reupload-orphan-fix-design.md#mechanism-of-the-leak"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0141", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B012-068", "B012-070"], "canonical_claim": "`PocoHTTPClient` applies `request_timeout_ms` as socket send/receive timeouts rather than one strict wall-clock deadline for the complete logical S3 operation.; An HTTP-attempt timeout is not the deadline for a complete logical CAS operation; CAS code owns retries, gates attempts on the local mount fence and remaining lease time, resolves uncertain writes from exact keys where permitted, and bounds retry budgets.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-s3-timeout-retry-control-rfc.md#current-behavior", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-s3-timeout-retry-control-rfc.md#summary"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0142", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B013-020"], "canonical_claim": "`CasGenerationSeal` decodes `RefNsCleanupState` and `TokenType` with unchecked `static_cast`, allowing invalid wire values to reach GC decision logic.", "issue_ids": ["U-minor"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup.md#L952-L1065", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-12-cas-stabilization-cleanup-design.md#L95-L99"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0143", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B019-009"], "canonical_claim": "The generic `clonePart` path uses `copyDirectoryContent` and `IDisk::copyFile` to create a fresh autocommit transaction per file, and a later content file raises `NOT_IMPLEMENTED` with `Autocommit writes are not supported for content part files`.", "issue_ids": ["S36"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-cas-move-to-ca.md#L338-L350"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0144", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B019-057", "B019-105", "B021-031", "B033-080"], "canonical_claim": "Review finding \u21161 is a partial real fix: conditional S3 copy can fall back to unconditional copying, but the common single-operation path is probe-guarded and the remaining gap is multipart copies larger than 32 MiB. The CAS review triage confirmed that conditional S3 copy could silently fall back to an unconditional write; task T8 fixed it in commit `a7d171f1d3e`. `copyObjectConditional` can fall back to an unconditional read/write copy after `AccessDenied` or unsupported multipart-copy paths, allowing a concurrent CAS promotion to be overwritten; conditional operations must fail closed. When `if_none_match` is present, both S3 copy fallback branches must rethrow the original error rather than degrade to an unconditional read/write copy.", "issue_ids": ["T8", "\u21161"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-codex-triage-fix-wave.md#L161-L178", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L149-L164", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L16-L23", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-19-session-full-summary.md#L10-L21", "docs/superpowers/reports/20260717_codex_review.md#blocker"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0145", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B019-075", "B019-099", "B033-098", "B040-108"], "canonical_claim": "Review finding \u211619 is a low-harm but real wire-contract issue: conditional mutations send only `Token.value`, so callers should reject mismatched token types before any conditional operation. Native conditional mutations ignore `Token.type` and send only `Token.value`, allowing a same-text token from a different token dialect to authorize a mutation. Emulated object tokens must use the underlying object's etag value with `TokenType::Emulated`, and conditional operations must reject an expected token whose type differs from the backend's minting type.; Persisted token values remain opaque strings and token_type, rather than provider-specific string shape, determines whether a token is ETag, generation, or emulated", "issue_ids": ["19c", "\u211618", "\u211619"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/codecs.md#token-subformat", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-codex-triage-fix-wave.md#L61-L80", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L367-L369", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L38-L39", "docs/superpowers/reports/20260717_codex_review.md#major-severity"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0146", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B019-080", "B019-108"], "canonical_claim": "Review finding \u211623 is real: CA `truncateFile` silently succeeds without changing bytes, so it should raise `NOT_IMPLEMENTED` because immutable blobs require whole-file replacement. CA `truncateFile` must throw `NOT_IMPLEMENTED` because blobs are immutable and whole-file rewrites replace the staged entry.", "issue_ids": ["\u211623"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-codex-triage-fix-wave.md#L194-L208", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L106-L110", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L43-L44"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0147", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B019-081", "B019-109"], "canonical_claim": "Review finding \u211624 is real: `unlinkFile` ignores `if_exists`, so removing a nonexistent file can silently succeed instead of raising `FILE_DOESNT_EXIST` for the non-`if_exists` API. CA `unlinkFile` must raise `FILE_DOESNT_EXIST` for a missing committed path when `if_exists` is false and be a no-op when `if_exists` is true.", "issue_ids": ["\u211624"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-codex-triage-fix-wave.md#L194-L208", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L112-L117", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-17-codex-review-triage.md#L44-L45"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0148", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M-080", "B019-112", "B020-016", "B020-018", "B020-019"], "canonical_claim": "CAS blob freshness-meta writes on the INSERT/merge hot path bypass the budgeted `CasRequestController`: `putMetaIfAbsent`, `casMeta`, and `deleteMetaExact` call backend conditional operations directly. S22 exposed a product bug: conditional freshness-meta sidecar writes for CAS blob keys such as `soak_pool/blobs/ch128/<xx>/<hash>.meta` bypassed the CAS retry controller, so an injected S3 `SlowDown` escaped as HTTP 500 with `S3_ERROR` code 499. `writeFreshMetaClean`, `writeResurrectMetaClean`, `putMetaIfAbsent`, and `casMeta` call `backend.casPut(...)` directly through `CasBlobMeta.cpp`, while `conditionalWriteSettings()` forces `s3_max_unexpected_write_error_retries_override = 1`, leaving freshness-meta writes with zero controller retries. A five-hour CA soak validation round found a genuine PRODUCT BUG in S22: `CasBlobMeta.cpp`'s `putMetaIfAbsent`/`casMeta`/`deleteMetaExact` hit the backend directly, the only hot-path conditional-write class outside `CasRequestController`, so an injected `SlowDown` fault gets one SDK attempt with zero controller-level retries and escapes to the client as an HTTP 500; the fix reroutes these through the controller and adds a new controlled If-Match variant plus a fault gtest.; Freshness-meta conditional writes must be routed through the shared `CasRequestController`, using controlled put-if-absent and controlled If-Match overwrite variants; transient errors must be absorbed inside the controlled call rather than swallowed as best-effort failures because stale meta state affects point readers.", "issue_ids": ["S22"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-17-codex-triage-fix-wave.md#L225-L253", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-18-s22-throttle-retry-rca.md#L1-L23", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-18-s22-throttle-retry-rca.md#L36-L56", "docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-18-s22-throttle-retry-rca.md#L58-L88", "docs/superpowers/worklogs/2026-07-17-unattended-r5-r6-round.md#L117-L122"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0149", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B026-053"], "canonical_claim": "The observed CAS ref-prefix enumeration omitted two objects that had been durable for nineteen seconds while returning a third object written 2.2 milliseconds after them; the store-side mechanism remains unknown.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-26-list-incompleteness-investigation.md#investigation"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0150", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B026-057"], "canonical_claim": "Historical and live holes form short adjacent runs rather than dropped pages: one historical firing had 13 holes across two namespaces, and the live capture had two adjacent holes immediately below the witness id `0x1430e`.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/2026-07-26-list-incompleteness-investigation.md#shape"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0151", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B033-093", "B044-028"], "canonical_claim": "Default CAS deduplication relies on collision-prone `CityHash128` without rehashing or comparing stored bytes, so an untrusted shared-pool writer can substitute attacker-controlled bytes after a chosen collision. Pool-global deduplication uses non-cryptographic `CityHash128` content keys without normal read-time payload rehashing, so a collision can poison a blob across tables or tenants that share a pool.", "issue_ids": ["SEC-1"], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/20260717_codex_review.md#high-severity", "docs/superpowers/reports/reviews.md#L935-L966"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-0152", "topic": "blob protocol contract", "target": "architecture/blob-protocol", "member_ids": ["B033-097"], "canonical_claim": "The emulated Local backend returns monotonic emulation tokens for exact operations but ETag/mtime tokens from LIST, so GC exact deletes based on listing tokens fail.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/reports/20260717_codex_review.md#major-severity"]}

